# A machine that declares no effects at all.
#
# `effects F { }` is an uninhabited enum. The interesting consequence is what
# it removes: with no effect to name, `EMIT` cannot be written here at all,
# because `EMIT()` is `tabula::empty-emit`. The whole vocabulary of this
# machine is IGNORE, GO, HANDLE and UNREACHABLE.
#
# `Open` has no static incoming transition -- the only route there is the
# HANDLE cell at (Locked, Unlock). That is legitimate, and it is why the
# reachability warning is gated on a fully-static matrix. This fixture pins
# the gate: if any implementation drops it, `effects-never.cov` fails.

machine Gate
initial Locked
states  Locked Open
actions Unlock Lock Push

Locked | HANDLE | IGNORE      | IGNORE
Open   | IGNORE | GO(Locked)  | HANDLE
